==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|es|Caribe}}, likely from an {{der|en|crb|-}} term, {{m|crb|karifuna||Island Carib person}} in modern Island Carib, a borrowing from a {{der|en|sai-car}} language (Island Carib itself being an Arawakan and ''not'' a Cariban language, despite the name), ultimately from {{der|en|sai-car-pro|*karipona||person}}. Compare {{cog|car|karìna||Carib person}}. {{doublet|en|cannibal|caribe|Garifuna|Carijona|Kari'na}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|en}}
{{rfap|en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|Carib}}

# A member of one of a number of [[Amerindian]] [[people]]s who [[inhabit]] the [[coast]] of [[Central America|Central]] and [[South America]] and the [[Lesser Antilles]].
## A member of the [[mainland]] or ‘[[proper]]’ {{w|Kalina people|Caribs}} ([[Kari'na]]), a [[Cariban]] people who inhabit the north [[coast]] of [[South America]], in parts of [[Venezuela]], [[Guyana]], [[Suriname]], and [[French Guiana]].
## A member of the {{w|Kalinago}} people of the [[Lesser Antilles]], an [[Arawakan]] people who took heavy [[cultural]] [[influence]] from the mainland Caribs and so were formerly known as [[Island Carib]]s.
## A member of the {{w|Garifuna}} people of [[Honduras]], historically known as [[Black Carib]]s, [[descendant]]s of mixed Kalinago people and [[African]]s who were [[deport]]ed to the [[Central America]]n mainland in the 18th century.

